# ICE Workflow — Intent, Contract, Evidence

Every change answers three questions: **what does it mean** (intent), **how do I know**
(contract), **where is the proof** (evidence). Production code does not change until all
three have an answer.

## Source of truth

- `doc/intent/` is the only truth about **meaning**. Read `status: current` nodes only.
- Reports, run artifacts and git history are **audit**, never specification.
- `doc/intent/MAP.md` is the routing map: always readable, used to find the right node.
- Everything else is read through a **slice**, not by browsing `doc/`.
- No `doc/intent/` in the project yet → work under the existing rules and offer to start
  the tree. Never invent a tree silently.

## Tooling

```bash
python3 .cursor/tools/intent/cli.py <command>   # in a project (template is a submodule)
python3 tools/intent/cli.py <command>           # inside the template repo itself
```

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `validate` | machine rules V1–V10 over the tree; exit 1 on error |
| `map` | regenerate `MAP.md` and `INDEX.json` (never edit them by hand) |
| `new --parent iNNNN --slug x` | allocate an id and scaffold a node |
| `slice iNNNN --for plan\|implement` | the file list for one action |
| `scope --run <dir>` | diff versus declared outputs (scope guard) |
| `coverage` | contracts without a machine enforcer; code outside any node |
| `owner <path>` | which node governs a file |

## Roles

| Role | May | May not |
|------|-----|---------|
| **Coordinator** (parent chat) | start other roles, pick models, count loops, allocate ids | write production code; grade its own output |
| **Planner** | intent deltas, run plan, slice, test spec | write production code; approve its own plan |
| **Critic** | verdict `ACCEPT` / `REVISE` on plans and intent changes | rewrite the plan; write code |
| **Coder** | production code, tests, report | change `current` nodes; start its own review |
| **Grader** | run `VERIFY.md` (machine, not an LLM) | interpret intent; weaken a test to pass |
| **Adversary** | `APPROVE` / `REQUEST CHANGES` on the diff | fix production code |

The Coder never starts the Adversary. The Adversary always uses a different model than
the Coder. Loops are bounded: after 3 rounds, escalate to the Human.

## Complexity

| Level | Definition |
|-------|------------|
| `low` | does **not** change the tree, stays inside one node's `code_paths`, adds no dependency and no public interface |
| `medium` | anything else that is not `high` |
| `high` | any deterministic trigger below |

Triggers forcing `high`: weakening or removing a contract; changing non-goals; retiring a
node; changing a node that has children; auth, cryptography or secrets; database
migration or schema change; changing an interface another node cites; adding or removing
a third-party dependency; deleting files; touching `.cursor/`, `hooks/`, CI or
`VERIFY.md`.

Coordinator may raise the level at any time. **Only the Human may lower it.**

## Gates

| Gate | low | medium | high |
|------|-----|--------|------|
| `intent validate` | yes | yes | yes |
| Grader (`VERIFY.md`) | yes | yes | yes |
| Scope guard (`intent scope`) | yes | yes | yes |
| Failing-test evidence for every new test | yes | yes | yes |
| Critic on the plan | no | yes | yes |
| Critic on an intent change | not applicable | yes | yes |
| Adversary | no | yes | yes |
| Human after the result | skipped, with a recorded reason | notified | required |

Scope guard failure raises the run to `medium` and wakes the Adversary, whatever the
original level was.

## Always the Human

- Weakening or removing a contract — an agent may tighten one, never loosen it.
- The first root of the tree, changes to non-goals, retiring a node.
- A contract with `enforced_by: review` (a contract without a test).
- `git commit`, `push`, merge, database migration, deleting data.
- Any escalation, lowering complexity, changing this methodology, `AGENT_MODELS.md`,
  `VERIFY.md` or the list of allowed MCP servers.

## Stop and escalate when

The request contradicts a `current` node and no approved intent change exists; the slice
is incomplete; a node in the slice has a blocking open question; a gate ran out of
rounds; a commit, push, migration, deletion or new tool server is needed.

## Model selection

Capability intent per role lives in `AGENT_MODELS.md` (see `00-model-policy.mdc`).
Never invent a model slug outside that catalog.
